{
  "title": "Vendure \u2014 ecommerce (8,144\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Vendure\nDomain: ecommerce | Scale: large | Stars: 8,144\nProblem: Teams building e-commerce platforms must choose between rigid SaaS solutions or assembling a DIY stack of services. Vendure provides an open-source, headless TypeScript commerce backend that is fully extensible via plugins without requiring core forks.\nTarget users: Enterprise e-commerce development teams, Backend/full-stack developers building custom storefronts, Agencies building headless commerce solutions, Teams requiring multi-channel commerce infrastructure\nCore features: GraphQL API for both storefront (shop) and admin channels; Plugin architecture for extending or overriding core behavior without patching; Built-in commerce primitives: catalog, orders, customers, promotions, tax, shipping, payments, stock; React-based admin dashboard; Multi-channel support from a single backend; Official plugins: email, asset server, job queue, security hardening, telemetry; CLI tooling for generating plugins and migrations; E2E test harness with programmable mock server\nIntegrations: Vendure Cloud (managed hosting), GraphiQL (API explorer plugin), Docker / Kubernetes (deployment targets)\nTech stack: React (admin dashboard) + Node.js, NestJS, TypeScript, GraphQL + TypeORM (supports SQL databases) + Node.js host-agnostic (Docker, Kubernetes, cloud, self-hosted)\nKey libraries: NestJS, GraphQL, TypeORM, Lerna, gql-tada, ESLint, Prettier, ts-node, Bun\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Plugin-first design allows extending or overriding any part of the system through stable contracts, avoiding the need to fork the core codebase.\n- Lerna monorepo structure cleanly separates core framework, official plugins, dashboard, CLI, and testing harness into independently versioned packages.\n- Dual GraphQL API surface (shop API and admin API) separates customer-facing and administrative concerns at the API layer.\n- Code generation (gql-tada, GraphQL type codegen) is built into the development workflow to maintain end-to-end type safety across the TypeScript stack.",
